h won't penetrate their defense. You'll overheat before they do.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Go back. Swap parts. Change moves. Different approach. The game won't tell you the answer. You figure it out or you lose. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Break The Cycle</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3400110/extras/c0d3d86bdae7033a2cf567f5cdabd54e.poster.avif?t=1766130309\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3400110/extras/c0d3d86bdae7033a2cf567f5cdabd54e.webm?t=1766130309\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3400110/extras/c0d3d86bdae7033a2cf567f5cdabd54e.mp4?t=1766130309\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Iron's running out. Every mech operates alone. They mine mining scraps. They hoard resources. They fight anyone who gets close. This is the cycle. Endless extraction until there's nothing left.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're Ironweld. You choose to break it. Build cooperation where there's only isolation. Unite mechs instead of fighting alone. Prove a better system works.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Some will join you. Some will fight you. Both require proving your approach works through combat.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3400110/extras/2829637a642a973c67210d1db7c92dc2.poster.avif?t=1766130309\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3400110/extras/2829637a642a973c67210d1db7c92dc2.webm?t=1766130309\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akama